What is High Purity Air-Operated Double-Diaphragm Pump?
High Purity Air-Operated Double-Diaphragm (AODD) pumps are specialized positive displacement pumps designed for applications demanding exceptional cleanliness and contamination control. These pumps utilize compressed air to actuate two flexible diaphragms, creating a pumping action that moves fluid through check valves without exposing it to lubricants or particulates from internal gears or pistons. They are constructed from high-purity materials such as PTFE (Polytetrafluoroethylene) and PE (Polyethylene), which offer superior chemical resistance and prevent leaching, making them critical for sensitive processes.

